  "redondo-beach": "Along the South Bay coast, Redondo Beach is served by California Water Service, which supplies a mix of imported water and West Coast Basin groundwater to homes from the pier to the Riviera. This coastal blend commonly carries noticeable hardness and a chlorine-type disinfectant, a combination that leaves its mark on kitchens and bathrooms. Neighbors here often battle spotty dishes, cloudy shower glass, and the dry-skin feeling that follows a shower even in the ocean air. Those dissolved minerals also settle inside water heaters and coffee makers, cutting their useful life. Adding a PurAgain system that removes up to 99% of contaminants delivers cleaner, softer water throughout the house.",
