  "downey": "Downey stands out for running one of the region's self-sufficient municipal systems, pumping nearly all of its water from city-owned wells that reach deep into the Central Groundwater Basin. Because this supply is almost entirely local groundwater rather than imported river water, it is naturally rich in dissolved minerals and reliably hard. That hardness is why so many Downey homeowners fight scale on their faucets, cloudy residue on glassware, and dry, tight-feeling skin after showering. The same minerals quietly coat the inside of water heaters and dishwashers, forcing them to work harder. PurAgain filtration removes up to 99% of contaminants, so families across the city enjoy softer, cleaner water at every tap.",
  "norwalk": "Situated in the southeast corner of Los Angeles County, Norwalk draws much of its supply from the mineral-heavy Central Groundwater Basin, blended with imported water when demand climbs. Groundwater from this basin tends to be firmly hard, and a disinfectant residual is maintained to keep it safe on the way to homes near the 5 and 605 freeways. Households routinely notice scale building on fixtures, spots left on dishes after washing, and skin and hair that feel stripped of moisture. Those minerals also settle inside appliances, shortening how long they last. Installing a PurAgain system removes up to 99% of contaminants and leaves water that tastes and feels far cleaner.",
